From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheKit <thekit@disroot.org>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:01:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] surfaceflinger: post task layers to the host directly

With persist.waydroid.direct_layers set, a task whose layers can all be
shown as-is is sent as a scene of its own buffers, skipping composition.
Anything else falls back to the composed frame, sent as a one-layer scene.

The host's read fences are merged into the buffers' release fences, so
producers don't reuse a buffer the host compositor may still read.

Change-Id: Iee192d4d3bfc7dc33f4f3b81229bcd7df54aafe7
